1.6.0: synthetic print placeholders - the shelf is no longer empty

Three print stocks ship in data/prints/, every one labeled synthetic in
stem, TITLE and blurb: synthetic_cine_print (projection look - teal
shadows, rolled highlights, crushed toe), synthetic_minilab (one-hour-
photo warmth and punch), synthetic_archival_neutral (near-neutral,
demonstrates the chain itself). Generated by tools/make_print_cubes.py
as parametric stylizations - measured from nothing, and honest about it
per the measured-versus-inspired vocabulary in PRESET_SOURCES. Measured
2383-class cubes supersede them when dropped into the library; the
staging catalog already lists those stems.

Plumbing: the resolver gains a second root (data/prints, overridable
with POLAJUICE_PRINTS); print cubes classify as process "print", so
-f synthetic_* is refused as camera film while --print resolves it by
name. The web stages the prints family, activating the Print selector
on the deployed page for the first time. Compat tests cover both
directions; the optional-stem staging message is now informational
rather than alarming.
